{
  // A second project over the files #1417 touched, because the whole
  // smoke-tests tree carries a pre-existing type-error backlog (~2180 errors)
  // that tsconfig.json never saw — its `include` covers only src/ and scripts/.
  // Adding the whole tree to tsconfig.json would red the gate with unrelated
  // work, and @ts-ignore / file exclusions are not the fix. This file is the
  // ratchet: it typechecks the merge-guard test seam now, and each follow-up
  // ticket adds its own clean files to `include` until the backlog is gone and
  // the tree can move into tsconfig.json.
  //
  // #1449 round 2 added the ledger-writer-shape / override-provenance files
  // below. `tsconfig.json` pins `"types": ["node"]`, which hides the Bun
  // globals every smoke test uses (`Bun.spawnSync`, `import.meta.dirname`, and
  // the `bun:test` module itself), so those three files carry a per-file
  // `bun-test` ambient type declaration rather than a project-wide `"types"`
  // widening — a project-wide change would silently retypes the other 100+
  // files this project has never checked. The declaration is the one in
  // `smoke-tests/lib/bun-test.d.ts`: it names only the two symbols these files
  // use, so it is an auditable surface, not `@types/bun`.
